    "updated_at": "2022-08-01T19:53:27Z",
    "body": "thanks @domenic.  I would have accepted many of your suggestions but for the fact GitHub keeps erroring out on me when I do so.  If it's not giving you trouble to merge, you can go ahead and do so, or I can make the changes in my local file and re-push.  Whichever you prefer.\r\n\r\nDefinitely want @cookiecrook, @jcsteh and @aleventhal.\r\n\r\nI mentioned in the PR, but many of the additions here were from feedback from @jcsteh and @alice - so if I have not done what was necessary to make sure they get credited as co-authors, I'd very much like to make sure they will be once this has been given its further review.\r\n\r\nI had mentioned that I would add some more examples/guidance to this PR, but now I'm wondering if MDN is not the place for that.  Does anyone have a preference for that?",
